+{"timestamp_utc":"2026-08-28T12:13:00Z","kind":"branch_progress","content":"Shared fact graph and master_guidance are empty. Decisive invariant route: partnership preserves area and unordered side-length multiset. For a convex quadrilateral with fixed cyclic side lengths a,b,c,d and area K>0, put theta=angle ABC, phi=angle CDA, X=ab sin(theta), Y=ab cos(theta), H=(c^2+d^2-a^2-b^2)/2. Area and the cosine law give cd sin(phi)=2K-X and cd cos(phi)=H+Y. Subtracting the identities X^2+Y^2=a^2b^2 and (2K-X)^2+(H+Y)^2=c^2d^2 gives a nondegenerate line in (X,Y), since K>0. It meets the circle in at most two points. Each point fixes theta, diagonal AC, and hence both component triangles by SSS, so at most two congruence classes per ordered side tuple, at most 48 overall. Therefore an infinite pairwise noncongruent partner sequence cannot exist."}
